  "reproduce": {
    "instructions": "Save the script as /tmp/voy_k040_codebook.py, fetch project-pinned inputs with python3 -m vs fetch, then run PYTHONPATH=. python3 /tmp/voy_k040_codebook.py from the repository root. It verifies input hashes and asserts full code-space uniqueness, segmentation and plaintext round trips.",
    "script": "\"\"\"A fixed, space-delimited, marker-free mixed-radix codebook control.\"\"\"\nimport hashlib,json,random,statistics,math\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom vs import corpus,ivtff,refcorpus\n\nBITS=('a','o','d','y','n','r','l','ch','sh')\nGALLOWS=('k','t','p','f','ckh','cth','cph','cfh')\nN=25000; SEEDS=(17,37,73)\nBOOKS=('it_dante','es_buenamor','en_paston','medieval_czech_01473c19')\n\ndef encode(mask,repeats,g):\n    # Gallow and e-run are ordinary optional slots, not compulsory terminators.\n    a=[BITS[i] for i in range(4) if mask&(1<<i)]\n    if g: a.append(GALLOWS[g-1])\n    a+=['e']*repeats\n    a += [BITS[i] for i in range(4,9) if mask&(1<<i)]\n    return ''.join(a)\n\ndef vocabulary():\n    codes=[encode(mask,r,g) for mask in range(1<<9) for r in range(3) for g in range(9) if mask or r or g]\n    assert len(codes)==13823 and len(set(codes))==len(codes)\n    # Ensure no cross-glyph ambiguity introduced by concatenating EVA-basic units.\n    for mask in range(1<<9):\n      for r in range(3):\n       for g in range(9):\n        if not (mask or r or g):continue\n        expected=[BITS[i] for i in range(4) if mask&(1<<i)]+([GALLOWS[g-1]] if g else [])+['e']*r+[BITS[i] for i in range(4,9) if mask&(1<<i)]\n        assert ivtff.segment(encode(mask,r,g))==expected\n    return codes\n\ndef stats(words, valid):\n    types=list(set(words)); result={}\n    for name,seq in [('tokens',words),('types',types)]:\n        segs=[ivtff.segment(w) for w in seq]\n        gc=[sum(g in GALLOWS for g in s) for s in segs]\n        ends=Counter(s[-1] for s in segs)\n        result[name]={'n':len(seq),'mean_length':sum(map(len,segs))/len(seq),\n           'repeated_glyph_share':sum(len(set(s))<len(s) for s in segs)/len(seq),\n           'adjacent_repeat_share':sum(any(a==b for a,b in zip(s,s[1:])) for s in segs)/len(seq),\n           'gallows_present_share':sum(n>0 for n in gc)/len(seq),\n           'multiple_gallows_share':sum(n>1 for n in gc)/len(seq),\n           'distinct_gallows_share':sum(len(set(s)&set(GALLOWS))>1 for s in segs)/len(seq),\n           'length_hist':dict(sorted(Counter(map(len,segs)).items())),\n           'top_final':ends.most_common(5), 'grammar_membership':sum(w in valid for w in seq)/len(seq)}\n    return result\n\ndef witness(name):\n    train,_=corpus.split_pages('practice',name)\n    ws=[w for p in train for line in p.lines if line.unit=='P' for w in line.words\n        if not ivtff.uncertain(w) and w.isascii() and w.isalpha() and w.islower()]\n    assert len(ws)>=N\n    return ws[:N]\n\ndef planted(words,codes,seed):\n    assert len(set(words))<=len(codes)\n    rng=random.Random(seed); shuffled=codes[:];rng.shuffle(shuffled)\n    # First occurrence assignment is independent of manuscript and reversible given the codebook.\n    table={w:shuffled[i] for i,w in enumerate(dict.fromkeys(words))}; reverse={v:k for k,v in table.items()}\n    encoded=[table[w] for w in words]\n    assert [reverse[w] for w in encoded]==words and len(table)==len(reverse)\n    return encoded, len(table)\n\nif __name__=='__main__':\n    codes=vocabulary();valid=set(codes)\n    stolfi=Counter(1+bin(mask).count('1') for mask in range(1<<9))\n    assert all(stolfi[k+1]==math.comb(9,k) for k in range(10))\n    # Spaces are structural: a+o and ao are both valid, so removing them is ambiguous.\n    assert {'a','o','ao'}<=valid\n    pins={e['id']:e for e in refcorpus.pins()}\n    for b in BOOKS:\n        with open(pins[b]['file'],'rb') as f: assert hashlib.sha256(f.read()).hexdigest()==pins[b]['sha256'],b\n    for w in ('zl','it'):\n        fn={'zl':'ZL3b-n.txt','it':'IT2a-n.txt'}[w]\n        h={'zl':'bf5b6d4ac1e3a51b1847a9c388318d609020441ccd56984c901c32b09beccafc','it':'7f27a8b0feed8f6de0a99900df6bf912dd1d295c38e5f830bac8b41c3f536fb5'}[w]\n        with open('data/raw/'+fn,'rb') as f: assert hashlib.sha256(f.read()).hexdigest()==h\n    out={'code_space':len(codes),'fixed_bits':BITS,'repeat_glyph':'e','gallows':GALLOWS,'n':N,'stolfi_9bit_type_length_counts':dict(sorted(stolfi.items())), 'unspaced_ambiguity':['a o','ao'], 'witnesses':{},'planted':{}}\n    for w in ('zl','it'):out['witnesses'][w]=stats(witness(w),valid)\n    for b in BOOKS:\n        words=' '.join(refcorpus.blocks_of(b)).split()[:N]; assert len(words)==N\n        out['planted'][b]={}\n        for seed in SEEDS:\n            enc,n=planted(words,codes,seed);out['planted'][b][seed]={'dictionary_size':n,'decoded_exact':True,'stats':stats(enc,valid)}\n    print(json.dumps(out,indent=2))\n"
  },
  "limitations": "The dictionary is built from the full planted plaintext and transmitted or shared as side information; exact round-trip demonstrates reversibility, not recovery of an unknown key or acceptable compression cost. Codeword assignment is random, not fitted for the Voynich manuscript, and no historical codebook is claimed. The slot inventory deliberately restricts spellings and gives a fixed alphabet and slot order; the low membership figure is a test of this toy, not of the entire family. The 25,000-token windows and seeds are limited, and the Voynich witnesses are different readings of the same manuscript. Public practice training is not held-out scoring, no page seed was accessed, and no formal cipher cell was ruled out."
}
